        "model": "gpt-6.1-sol"
      },
      "text": "Sunday – Caracas and the Santa Teresa Estate"
    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:2e780f63f4172747",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "99366ae9e797e75013134d8f5c40e73aad8d7b9fdb2b2ac0fa874c8468237fd9",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-worker-d585b2821829f1fdbfcb5695",
        "model": "gpt-6.1-sol"
      },
      "text": "After breakfast, transfer to the airport and fly to Caracas. You will be met on arrival and head to the town of La Victoria.\n\nThe Santa Teresa Estate lies in a valley where sugar cane is grown. Martín Tovar Blanco founded the estate in 1796. In 1802, the King of Spain granted the Tovar family a princely title in recognition of the quality of their rum.\n\nThe tour takes you through the sugar cane plantations and historic buildings, with stops at the house museum that tells the story of the Creole Tovar family and the Criadero de Solera cellar. You then see the modern production facilities and taste the rum.\n\nThere is time to shop at the gift shop. Recommended choices include Santa Teresa 1796 rum and Araku coffee rum.\n\nLunch is at your own expense. After visiting the estate, you return to Caracas.\n\n**Meals:** breakfast."
    },
